                "title": "Sizable Energy plans offshore gravity storage projects in Italy - Energy Storage",
                "url": "https://www.ess-news.com/2026/11/10/sizable-energy-plans-offshore-gravity-storage-projects-in-italy",
                "source": "ess-news.com",
                "summary": "Floating offshore wind is another potential application. Sizable Energy says its storage system could share export cables with offshore wind farms, allowing the connection to be sized closer to average rather than peak generation. Excess electricity could then be stored offshore and exported when cable capacity becomes available, reducing connection costs and curtailment.\n\nFrom pv magazine Italia\n\n### More about\n\n Energy Storage\n LDES\n\n### Written by\n\n \n\n  Sergio Matalucci [...] ### Ocean storage\n\nSizable Energy’s platform is designed to integrate with floating solar and offshore wind. Floating solar panels could share infrastructure, moorings and grid connection cables with the storage reservoirs. The company’s Power Shell concept also combines offshore storage, floating solar and data centers on a single platform. [...] In Italy, Biondi identified Terna’s Macse mechanism, which provides long-term contracts for storage capacity, as a potential framework for grid-connected projects. Sizable Energy is also exploring direct renewable power supply agreements with large consumers, including data centers, to secure long-term revenue.",
